# roshambo.docshock.studio: the web game, on the Contabo server it shares with docshock.studio,
# purelyfreefonts.com and walnutbutter.ai.
#
# Edit it here, never on the server: deploy/deploy.sh --go puts it at /etc/caddy/sites/roshambo.caddy
# and reloads Caddy, and if Caddy refuses it, puts the old one back. The server's main Caddyfile
# (the purelyfreefonts repo's ops/Caddyfile) imports it, and its global options (which Cloudflare
# addresses to trust for the visitor's IP) apply here too.
#
# Cloudflare proxies the hostname and holds the public certificate. Caddy uses docshock.studio's
# Cloudflare Origin CA certificate, which also names *.docshock.studio, so it never asks Let's
# Encrypt for one. The server's firewall lets in only Cloudflare, so the DNS record has to be
# proxied (orange cloud).
#
# The game (roshambo/web.py, run by deploy/roshambo-web.service on localhost only) sets its own
# security headers and caching, and marks every response no-transform, so Cloudflare changes nothing
# on the way. Visits aren't logged, here or by the game.

roshambo.docshock.studio {
	tls /etc/caddy/certs/docshock.pem /etc/caddy/certs/docshock.key
	header -Server
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8777
}
